00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.120 align:start position:0%
workers start by adding the raw  materials to a mixer beginning with clay  [Music]  they had a fiber derived from ground-up  rice husks this fiber reinforces the  clay giving it added strength and  helping to prevent the finished product  from cracking at high temperatures  a craftsman places the clay inside a  specially shaped mold which sits on a  potter's wheel as the wheel turns the  mold the craftsman works with the metal  arm and handheld tools to spread and  shape the clay  [Music]  he then removes the fully-formed clay  pod  the craftsman now uses a handheld tool  to define and finish the edges of the  rim and supports he then uses a metal  rectangular template to mark and cut out  a small vent for air intake at the base  of the pot an artisan prepares a small  disc of clay for a different stage of  production he uses a cylindrical metal  tool to cut a series of 61 holes in the  disc creating a honeycomb pattern that  will allow the passage of air he is a  small beveled wooden tool to help smooth  the edges of the holes when the pots are  fully formed workers transfer them to  the walk-in oven once there are a total  of 500 pots and honeycombs inside it's  time to fire up the oven to assemble the  barbecues a worker starts by creating a  layer of rice husk between the clay pot  and the zinc bucket this insulates the  metal from the barbecues heat he cuts  out the rectangular vent that will allow  air to flow into the bottom of the  barbecue and help fuel the fire  he adds soil to the gap between the pot  and the bucket to further insulate the  exterior metal from the interior heat  [Music]  the craftsman now seals all the gaps in  the barbecue was mortar in order to keep  the husk and soil firmly in place  [Music]  the honeycomb disc fits perfectly into  the bottom of the pot it will hold  charcoal up above the vent hole allowing  air to flow up through it and fueling  the fire while permitting ash to fall  down into the cavity below a worker  carefully warders the disc in place this  barbecue is a low-tech but highly  effective outdoor stove useful whenever  it's too hot to cook inside
 

